p.m:
\displaystyle{\begin{aligned}
    3\cdot\left( -{\frac{2}{3}} \right)
    \amp =\frac{3}{1} \cdot \left(-{\frac{2}{3}}\right) \amp \hbox{We can divide both the first numerator and the second denominator by 3.}\\
    \amp =\frac{1}{1} \cdot \left(-{\frac{2}{1}}\right)\\
    \amp ={-2}
    \end{aligned}}
